Both demonstrations are present and labelled ("MUTATION 1 of 2 ... :491",
  "MUTATION 2 of 2 ... :468"). Each has assertion-level FAIL lines confined to its
  own case, and each ends with "mutant N exit: 1". These FAIL lines match my
  independent reruns exactly (same labels, same observed values 0/"").
Restoration is verified inline, in two ways:
  (1) The script reverts with git checkout between mutants. The log proves it
      took, by behaviour: in the mutant-2 run, "--decision of ../leges/qa"
      PASSes, which would not happen if mutant 1 were still applied.
  (2) A final "git diff -- lifecycle.ts" prints empty.
The harness still exists at the path the header names
  (session scratchpad .../54cefaf8-.../scratchpad/w042-mutants.sh). I read it.
  It does what the log says: sed of the exact line, ONLY=19 run, git checkout,
